# Kamailio dispatcher destinations (plan contract 7): set 1 is every
# hello-sip node, by its fixed IP on the edge network. Format:
#   setid destination flags priority attributes
# Flags 0: start active; probing (ds_probing_mode 1) then keeps each
# destination's state from its OPTIONS answers. Addresses, not names:
# Kamailio resolves names through Docker's DNS only (it ignores
# extra_hosts), a stopped container has no DNS record, and with
# ds_load_mode 1 an unresolvable entry is fatal at startup, so a restart
# while one node is down would take the whole edge down. An IP always
# loads; a stopped node is simply probed inactive until it answers again.
# The duid is the compose service name. Phase 6 replaces this file with a
# dynamic source.
1 sip:10.89.53.11:5060 0 0 duid=hello-sip-1
1 sip:10.89.53.12:5060 0 0 duid=hello-sip-2
